      "text": "The script finds the value-weighted monthly section, parses the six 2x3 portfolio columns, and computes HML as 0.5\u00b7(Small Value + Big Value) \u2212 0.5\u00b7(Small Growth + Big Growth), using the Ken French convention. The result is written to output.csv.\n\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\n\n\ndef is_yyyymm(tok):\n    return len(tok) == 6 and tok.isdigit()\n\n\ndef main():\n    with open(\"6_Portfolios_2x3.csv\", encoding=\"latin-1\") as f:\n        lines = f.read().splitlines()\n\n    # Locate the value-weighted monthly section (not the equal-weighted one)\n    start = None\n    for i, line in enumerate(lines):\n        low = line.lower()\n        if \"value weighted returns\" in low and \"monthly\" in low and \"equal\" not in low:\n            start = i\n            break\n    if start is None:\n        raise RuntimeError(\"Could not find value-weighted monthly section\")\n\n    rows = []\n    seen_data = False\n    for line in lines[start + 1:]:\n        if line.strip() == \"\":\n            if seen_data:\n                break\n            continue\n        parts = [p.strip() for p in line.split(\",\")]\n        if is_yyyymm(parts[0]):\n            seen_data = True\n            vals = []\n            for p in parts[1:7]:\n                try:\n                    v = float(p)\n                except ValueError:\n                    v = np.nan\n                if v != v or np.isclose(v, -99.99) or np.isclose(v, -999.0):\n                    v = np.nan\n                vals.append(v)\n            if len(vals) < 6:\n                vals += [np.nan] * (6 - len(vals))\n            rows.append([int(parts[0])] + vals)\n        else:\n            if seen_data:\n                break  # next section reached\n\n    cols = [\"date\", \"SL\", \"MB1\", \"SH\", \"BL\", \"MB2\", \"BH\"]\n    df = pd.DataFrame(rows, columns=cols)\n\n    # Ken French HML: average of the two value portfolios minus average of the two growth portfolios\n    df[\"value\"] = 0.5 * (df[\"SH\"] + df[\"BH\"]) - 0.5 * (df[\"SL\"] + df[\"BL\"])\n\n    out = df[[\"date\", \"value\"]].dropna().copy()\n    out[\"date\"] = out[\"date\"].astype(int)\n    out.to_csv(\"output.csv\", index=False)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
